From f78a397c0b8051d70d60516402a35a9df9ffc289 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VERHILLE Arnaud <gist974@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 13:52:56 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 01/20] Serve the expired DBcc and trapping TRAPV refill from
 the instruction cache

On the 68020 core, an expired DBcc and a trapping TRAPV read the program
word at PC + 2 and discard it, like MOVE to SR/CCR. With an emulated
instruction cache, that read now goes through readStatusRefill() as well,
so a cached word costs no bus access.

In the cache case, MC68020UM 8.2.15 gives DBcc (cc = False, Count
Expired) 10(0/0/0) and 8.2.17 gives TRAPV (Trap) 25(1/0/5): no prefetch
(instruction access). MC68030UM 11.6.15 and 11.6.17 give 10(0/0/0) and
22(1/0/5) for the I-cache case.

The discarded read of TRAPV is Moira's model, not a statement of the
manuals: both tables give a trapping TRAPV the prefetches of TRAP #n,
which reads no such word. Only the absence of an instruction access in
the cache case is cited for it.

Without MOIRA_EMULATE_ICACHE the read stays a bus access, as before. With
an emulated cache that CACR has disabled, the word now comes through
readInstr(): it costs no bus access when the one-longword latch holds it,
although the no-cache columns count three prefetches for the expired DBcc
(10(0/3/0) and 13(0/3/0)); a word that is fetched is charged as an
instruction fetch, and a bus error on it takes the instruction fetch path.
The MOVE to SR/CCR refill has the same property.
---
 Moira/MoiraDataflow.h | 2 +-
 Moira/MoiraExec_cpp.h | 4 ++--
 2 files changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Moira/MoiraDataflow.h b/Moira/MoiraDataflow.h
index 9bb4dc1..b694bda 100644
--- a/Moira/MoiraDataflow.h
+++ b/Moira/MoiraDataflow.h
@@ -114,7 +114,7 @@ template <Core C, Size S, Flags F = 0> u32 readDataCache(u32 addr);
 template <Core C, Flags F = 0> u16 readInstr(u32 addr);
 
 
-// Reads the instruction word discarded by MOVE to SR or CCR.
+// Reads the instruction word discarded by MOVE to SR or CCR, an expired DBcc or a trapping TRAPV.
 template <Core C> void readStatusRefill();
 
 // Writes an operand to memory (without or with address error checking)
diff --git a/Moira/MoiraExec_cpp.h b/Moira/MoiraExec_cpp.h
index 2bfbf94..3cd07b7 100644
--- a/Moira/MoiraExec_cpp.h
+++ b/Moira/MoiraExec_cpp.h
@@ -2464,7 +2464,7 @@ Moira::execDbcc(u16 opcode)
             } else {
 
                 writeD<Word>(dn, U32_SUB(readD<Word>(dn), 1));
-                (void)read<C, AddrSpace::PROG, Word>(reg.pc + 2);
+                readStatusRefill<C>();
                 CYCLES_68020(10);
                 fullPrefetchAt<C, POLL>(reg.pc + 2);
             }
@@ -5514,7 +5514,7 @@ Moira::execTrapv(u16 opcode)
 
         } else {
 
-            (void)read<C, AddrSpace::PROG, Word>(reg.pc + 2);
+            readStatusRefill<C>();
             SYNC(2);
         }
 
